182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (The fog harvesting research project explored how fog can provide an alternative source of water through the development of a symmetrical fog harvester and a climate simulation model. By testing at Kennesaw Mountain and Mount Oglethorpe, I compared the predicted fog yields with actual collected water. The results showed that while the model could estimate fog collection under certain conditions, it was not always accurate. Overall, this project demonstrated the potential of fog harvesting and the importance of improving the model to better predict water collection in different environments.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
